      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:white_hole_emitter",
      "title": "White Hole Emitter",
      "text": "A black hole, run backwards in time. Nothing can enter; everything comes out. The $(item)White Hole Emitter$() should not work. It does.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Theory check: the equations of general relativity are time-symmetric, so every black hole solution has a reversed twin - a $(thing)white hole$(), a horizon that can only be left, never crossed inward. None has ever been observed. Its lensing ring, I note, behaves the opposite way to a black hole's."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
